            <ArticleTitle>The Cheshire Cat Syndrome: an unusual case of neurosarcoidosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>149-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Clinical diagnosis of neurosarcoidosis depends on the finding of neurological disease in a patient with biopsy proven multisystem sarcoidosis. Without the biopsy evidence, solitary central nervous system sarcoidosis remains a difficult diagnosis. In some cases, only a long-term follow-up will establish the diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
